    // Point sets for ConvexHullTests.
    //
    // These point sets are kept as static definitions because nearly all of them failed with ComputeHull as it was
    // before (gift wrapping), or with an earlier version of the hull that replaced it, and they failed in different
    // ways: hulls left open (their faces' area vectors not cancelling, by up to 38 % of the area), points left outside
    // the hull, and faces whose vertices lie off their own planes. Keeping every one of them here was the easiest way
    // to make sure none of those failures comes back in the future. The few gift wrapping got right are kept to show
    // that what worked still works.
    //
    // Most ("Chopped") are the vertices of convex pieces chopped off meshes in a game: many nearly coplanar points,
    // in clusters a fraction of a millimetre apart. The rest are ConvexHullTestDemo's own point sets. Each set's
    // comment says how gift wrapping handled it.
    public partial class ConvexHullTests
    {
